# Read global AGENTS.md

Cursor already loads every rule in `~/.cursor/rules` and the open project's `.cursor/rules`. It does not load a user-level `AGENTS.md` by itself.

At the start of each task, read and follow `~/.cursor/AGENTS.md`. That file is the global instruction file. Codex and Claude Code load the same bytes from their own filenames.

Apply all of these together:

- `~/.cursor/AGENTS.md`
- every other rule in `~/.cursor/rules`
- the project's `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules`

When a project instruction conflicts with the global file, follow the project.

```text
❌ BAD
Follow only the project's .cursor/rules and skip ~/.cursor/AGENTS.md.

✅ GOOD
Read ~/.cursor/AGENTS.md, then apply it together with ~/.cursor/rules and the project's rules. The project wins on conflict.
```
